-# How a set is drafted and what you build out of it. Anything but the normal
-# draft comes from the comprehensive rules - Commander Draft is 903.13,
-# Conspiracy Draft is 905, Two-Headed Giant drafting is not in the rules,
-# but how it is played is 810.
- case limited_format.play_variant
- when "commander"
  = render "commander_draft_rules", limited_format: limited_format
- when "multiplayer"
  %p
    From every booster, draft one card, and pass the rest to the next player,
    until all cards have been drafted.
    Direction changes with every booster.
  %p
    Some cards are drafted face up, or ask you to reveal them and note something
    as you draft them, and cards in the game care about what happened.
  %p
    From cards you draft and any number of basic land cards, build a 40 card deck.
    Conspiracy cards are never part of your deck - as the game begins you may put
    any number of the ones you drafted into the command zone instead, face down if
    they have hidden agenda.
  %p
    Games are played as free-for-all multiplayer, and you can attack multiple players.
    = link_to "See rule 905 for the full rules.", controller: "help", action: "rules", anchor: "section-905"
- when "two-headed-giant"
  %p
    You draft in a team of two, and the packs above are what your team gets
    between the two of you. Your team opens a booster, drafts two cards, and
    passes the rest to the next team.
    Direction changes with every booster.
  %p
    Cards your team drafts are one shared pool, and are not assigned to either of
    you as you draft them. From that pool and any number of basic land cards,
    each of you builds their own 40 card deck. Cards you don't use are a shared
    sideboard.
  = render "two_headed_giant_play"
- else
  %p
    From every booster, draft one card, and pass the rest to the next player,
    until all cards have been drafted.
    Direction changes with every booster.
  %p
    From cards you draft and any number of basic land cards, build a 40 card deck.
